            "heading": "Logic and Shift Instructions",
            "anchor": "logic-and-shift-instructions",
            "startLine": 14236,
            "endLine": 14255
          },
          "quotation": "The logic and shift instructions are fundamentally untyped, performing bit-wise operations on operands of any type, provided the operands are of the same size. This permits bit-wise operations on floating point values without having to define a union to access the bits."
        },
