            "heading": "Fundamental Types",
            "anchor": "fundamental-types",
            "startLine": 3062,
            "endLine": 3066
          },
          "quotation": "Most instructions have one or more type specifiers, needed to fully specify instruction behavior. Operand types and sizes are checked against instruction types for compatibility.\nTwo fundamental types are compatible if they have the same basic type and are the same size. Signed and unsigned integer types are compatible if they have the same size. The bit-size type is compatible with any fundamental type having the same size."
        },
