            "anchor": "ptx-instructions",
            "startLine": 7513,
            "endLine": 7527
          },
          "quotation": "PTX instructions generally have from zero to four operands, plus an optional guard predicate appearing after an @ symbol to the left of the opcode:\n@p opcode;\n@p opcode a;\n@p opcode d, a;\n@p opcode d, a, b;\n@p opcode d, a, b, c;\nFor instructions that create a result value, the d operand is the destination operand, while a, b, and c are source operands."
        },
